 ## Overview
-Density Voxel Grid Reconstruction is a method for generating high-quality 3D reconstructed scenes and novel view images from 2D RGB inputs, specifically designed to operate after camera pose optimization [S1]. It replaces the Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) used in traditional Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) or the sparse voxels with spherical harmonics used in Plenoxels, utilizing a dense density voxel grid for the final reconstruction stage [S1]. This approach is particularly effective in scenarios where input camera poses contain significant noise, as it relies on poses that have been refined by preceding optimization steps [S1].
